Short:        DVD-Video navigation library (libdvdnav)
Author:       Brian King; libdvdread and libdvdnav by VideoLAN et al.
Uploader:     Brian King
Type:         util/libs
Version:      1.7
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     68020+
Replaces:     -

dvdnav.library gives any program DVD-Video navigation: VideoLAN's
libdvdread 7.1.1 and libdvdnav 7.0.0, the libraries VLC, mpv and Kodi
play DVDs with, as an Exec library.

- The program reads the disc (a drive's sectors, or an image file)
  through a reader it gives the library.
- The library reads the disc's file system and IFOs, runs the DVD's
  virtual machine (menus, buttons, titles, chapters, angles, still
  frames) and hands back the MPEG-2 Program Stream one 2048-byte block at
  a time, with events for stills, palettes, streams, highlights and
  jumps. Decoding and drawing are the program's.
- 68020 or better, no FPU needed. About 30 KB of the caller's stack when
  a title is opened: call it from a process with 48 KB.
- CSS-scrambled discs only with an optional libdvdcss library, which is
  not part of this archive.

Contents:
  dvdnav/Libs/dvdnav.library             copy to LIBS:
  dvdnav/Include/                        the headers, for programmers
  dvdnav/dvdnav_lib.sfd                  the functions
  dvdnav/README.md, CHANGES

Licence: the library is GPL-3.0-or-later (libdvdread and libdvdnav are
GPL-2.0-or-later: COPYING.libdvdread, COPYING.libdvdnav); its source is
at

  https://github.com/luvwagn/dvdnav.library

The headers and the .sfd are MIT, so any program may be built against
them and open the library at run time.

Made for Ambiance, an Amiga Media Center application
(formerly amcedvd.library there).
